# Project Build & Run Guide

This guide explains how to format, build, and run the project across platforms and also showcases the current rendering output and threading layout used in the path tracer.

## Code Formatting

```bash
clang-format.exe -i src/*.h src/*.cpp
```

## Windows: Build

```powershell
set VCPKG_ROOT="$HOME/vcpkg"
vcpkg install
vcpkg integrate install
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE="${VCPKG_ROOT}/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake"
cmake --build build
```

## macOS: Build

```bash
brew install vcpkg
brew install pkg-config
git clone https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg "$HOME/vcpkg"
export VCPKG_ROOT="$HOME/vcpkg"
vcpkg install
vcpkg integrate install
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE="${VCPKG_ROOT}/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake"
cmake --build build
```

## Debug Build

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE="${VCPKG_ROOT}/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
cmake --build build
```

## Release Build

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE="${VCPKG_ROOT}/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build
```

## Run (after a successful build)

```bash
cd build
./helloworld
```

## Sample Output

Sphere layout overview:
- Ground plane: large diffuse sphere at `(0, -1000, 0)`.
- Ring of diffuse spheres: 12 objects of radius `0.62`, resting at `y = rObj` on a circle of radius `R`.
- Overhead emissive ring: 12 light spheres of radius `0.5` at `y = 6`, each emitting colored light.

```cpp
// Ring scene layout:
const int   N = 12;
const float R = 2.55f;  // ring radius, gap between spheres
const float rObj = 0.62f;
const float objectY = rObj; // diffuse spheres rest on the ground plane
const float lightY = 6.0f;
const float rLight = 0.5f;
const float emission = 30.0f;
``` 

